{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Paul stood in the middle of the Areo[Eb]pagus
Saw the [Gm]city full of i[F]dols all around [Eb]
[Bb]He looked at the objects of their wor[Eb]ship
And found an al[Gm]tar [F]with a hidden [Eb]sound
To an [Gm]unknown god [F]it was in[Eb]scribed
What you wor[Gm]ship in ig[F]norance I will ex[Eb]plain
The [Bb]God who made the world and everything [Eb]in it
Does not [Gm]live in temples made [F]by human [Eb]hands
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
He gives everyone life and breath [F]and all things
From [Gm]one man he made every na[Eb]tion
To seek God and perhaps reach [F]out for him
Though he is [Gm]not far from [F]any one of [Eb]us
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
In [Bb]him we live and move and have our be[Eb]ing
We [Gm]are his offspring as [F]the poets say [Eb]
So we ought [Bb]not to think that the di[Eb]vine being
Is like [Gm]gold or silver [F]shaped by human [Eb]skill
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Gm7] [F] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
God [Bb]overlooked the times [F]of ignorance [Eb]past
But [Gm]now he commands [F]all people [Eb]to repent
He has [Bb]set a day to judge [F]the world with [Eb]justice
By the man [Gm]he has appoint[F]ed for the [Eb]end
He has given proof of this to every[F]one
By [Gm]raising him from the [F]dead in glory's [Eb]light
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm7]Some began to mock when they [F]heard of the resurrection
[Gm]But others said [F]we will hear you a[Eb]gain
[Cm7]Damaris joined him [F]and came to believe
A [Gm]woman from [F]Athens in [Eb]the center of the [Bb]plan
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
And [Gm]others with them [F]believed in the [Eb]risen Lord
The [Gm]gospel reached the [F]mind and the [Eb]heart of man
{end_of_verse}

